  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Lawrence Butler's error in the seventh broke a tie the Athletics should have kept intact. They led through six innings with a pitcher who had given them air to breathe. That lead did not survive contact with reality.",
    "what_this_means": "J.T. Ginn threw six solid innings. Three earned runs on five hits, five strikeouts. The offense answered with production when it mattered: two runs on two RISP conversions across seven opportunities. That should be enough. Cincinnati scored twice in the eighth and once more in the ninth. The Athletics never recovered. The bullpen could not hold. Hogan Harris gave up both eighth-inning runs in 0.2 innings. By the time anyone got warm, the game was gone. This is not inconsistency. This is a team that cannot afford the mistakes it keeps making. Down 13 games in the division with six weeks left, they need clean baseball. They delivered sloppy. Eight left on base. One win in nine games.",
    "what_to_watch": "Rhett Lowder takes the mound tonight against Jacob Lopez, whose ERA sits at 1.75 over his last four starts. The Athletics need Lopez to be exactly what he has become.",
